"""
## Purpose and audience
Phase 5 of the markdown editor: executable evidence for the block model, the
markdown renderer, syntax highlighting, and the editor wiring (preview pane,
commands, diagnostics, TUI/GUI shells). Written for the editor team that owns
src/lib/editor/ and for reviewers verifying markdown preview behavior.
## Operator workflow
Run `simple run test/03_system/gui/editor_markdown_spec.spl` and confirm only
the documented RED below fails. Structural scenarios read the shipped module
sources through read_text; behavioral scenarios call the real renderer, table,
callout, wiki-index, and diagnostics functions.
## Compatibility and limitations
Known RED by contract: "markdown language extension exposes IDE command
routing" — md_language.spl does not yet register ExtensionCommand entries for
md.preview/md.toggleBold/md.toggleItalic; keep that scenario failing until the
extension registers those commands. Interface scenarios assert the shipped
source contracts (declaration text) of src/lib/editor/ modules.
## Verification guidance and troubleshooting
Re-run the single spec file; each failing line's `# oracle:` comment states
why the pinned value is correct. Source-contract failures mean the named
declaration moved or was renamed in src/lib/editor/.
# @manual: primary
REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM
doc/01_research/domain/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md
doc/03_plan/sspec_modernization_plan.md
doc/04_architecture/sspec_documentization_maintenance.md
doc/05_design/infra/sspec/modern_sspec_typed_evidence_design.md
"""
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-SYSTEM
# @manual_section: markdown editor rendering

